<title>UK: LPC - Cable &amp; Wireless mandates four for stg credit.</title>
<headline>LPC - Cable &amp; Wireless mandates four for stg credit.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, February 21 (LPC) - Cable &amp; Wireless have mandated Chase Investment Bank, Citibank, HSBC and Toronto-Dominion Bank to arrange the 2.9 billion stg credit supporting the complex merger of four cable companies, bankers said.</p>
<p>The merger of Cable &amp; Wireless's Mercury Communications with Nynex CableComms, Bell Cablemedia and Videotron will create Britain's biggest cable company.</p>
<p>The credit will be used to combine the four companies' existing debt into one jumbo facility, bankers said. The newly merged entity, which was cleared by the European Commission on December 11, will be known as Cable and Wireless Communications.</p>
<p>LPC Newsroom 44-0171-542-4048</p>
</text>
